From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@mono.si>
Date: Sat, 25 Apr 2026 17:55:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] soc: fsl: qbman: skip KASAN instrumentation

The SDK copy's Makefiles (sdk_fman, sdk_dpaa and staging/fsl_qbman in
sdk/linux) turn KASAN instrumentation off: those drivers do plain
memset()/memcpy() on iomem (MURAM and QBMan portal regions), and with
CONFIG_KASAN_GENERIC=y the instrumented calls look up shadow an iomem
address does not have, and fault. The change that did so opted
mainline's QBMan driver out with them; this is that line.

KASAN_SANITIZE := n suppresses only the compiler's instrumentation of
these objects. KASAN stays enabled, so a caller's kmalloc'd buffer passed
down is still checked.

ASK's kernel config builds the SDK's QBMan, not this one (CONFIG_FSL_DPAA
is off): the line matters only to a kernel that builds mainline's QBMan
as well.

Signed-off-by: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@mono.si>
---
 drivers/soc/fsl/qbman/Makefile | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/fsl/qbman/Makefile b/drivers/soc/fsl/qbman/Makefile
index 811312ad526fb..4ee2a84159f0d 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/fsl/qbman/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/soc/fsl/qbman/Makefile
@@ -1,4 +1,6 @@
 # SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
+KASAN_SANITIZE := n
+
 obj-$(CONFIG_FSL_DPAA)                          += bman_ccsr.o qman_ccsr.o \
 						   bman_portal.o qman_portal.o \
 						   bman.o qman.o dpaa_sys.o
-- 
